    {
      "ordinal": 7,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "1.4",
      "title": "Wooden shields requirements",
      "body": "● The entire edge must be covered with either a band of strong leather, or with at least three or more layers of fabric.\n● A leather band must be glued, sewn or riveted, to the shield. Any rivets must be neatly finished, the edge of the rivet should not stick out.\n● The flat outside wooden shields must be covered with leather or fabric.\n● The handles must be made of leather.\n● Wooden bucklers and Heater shields with a central handle must have a handle made of wood.\n● Shield boss (umbo) made of metal must conform to the Armors and weapons Aesthetics and decorations document.",
      "page_from": 4,
      "page_to": 4,
