    {
      "ordinal": 8,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "1.5",
      "title": "Metal shields requirements",
      "body": "● Must be of round shapes, based on historical sources, and repeat the form of the original in all three dimensions.\n● The entire edge of metal shields must be rolled to the thickness of a minimum of 4 mm or more.\n● The handles must be made of metal and or wood\n● Metal shields and shield boss (umbo) must conform to the Armors and weapons Aesthetics and decorations document.\n● It is allowed to blacken the back part of a metal shield or metal buckler. Example:\n\nPicture from O. Haguenstein ©",
