    {
      "ordinal": 10,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "2.1",
      "title": "Historical sources and datation",
      "body": "● Heater shields are the main shield shape for knights of the middle ages. Its triangular shape is typical of the 14th century. The shape goes thinner as the armors become more effective.\n● They are approved for 14th century, Transitional and 15th century armors.\n\nShield of Loew von Steinfurth - 1380 - Germany Grande Chroniques de France - 1400 - France\n\nPolitica & Economica - 1376 - France Ab Urbe Condita - 1390/1400 - France",
      "page_from": 5,
      "page_to": 5,
